"Waves come, and waves flow,\nWaves at us, as they go.\n\nMakes us love 'em, as they show\nCare for us, which then flow.\n\nThough they feel good, they're not our,\nThe surface is reachable, the bed's too far.\n\nNot every water, is meant for us,\nNot every drop, is drinkable.\nTheir true love, are the fish,\nYou can't have a place, for life's not a fable.\n\nCrocodile gets the saltwater,\nGator gets the fresh,\nGharial goes fresh and deep,\nYou've no place for the river, go deep and lose your flesh.\n\nSo work on yourself,\nDon't thrive water,\nFor we are not swimmers, never meant to be,\nThose waves are just, distracting starters."